.TH ROTBYTE 1 "2026-04-08" "rotbyte 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rotbyte \- detect bit rot by tracking BLAKE2b checksums
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rotbyte
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rotbyte
computes BLAKE2b-512 checksums for every file in a directory tree and
stores them in a local SQLite database. On subsequent runs it detects
silent data corruption (bit rot) by comparing stored checksums against
freshly computed ones.
.PP
By default, only files whose size or modification time have changed are
re-hashed. Use
.B \-\-check
to force a full re-verify of every file, which is the only way to catch
true bit rot (corruption without metadata change).
.PP
The database is created automatically as
.BI . dirname _checksums.db
inside the target directory on first run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Force re-hash of every file regardless of modification time.
.TP
.B \-\-report
Print an integrity status summary and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-accept " FILE"
Accept a single file's current state as correct. If the file is MISSING,
its record is removed. If FAILED, it is re-hashed and the new checksum
becomes the known-good baseline.
.TP
.B \-\-accept\-all
Accept all current state as the new baseline. Clears all MISSING records
and re-hashes all FAILED files.
.TP
.B \-\-import
Import existing
.I .b2sum
and
.I .b2
hash files into the database. Verifies each hash matches the file on disk
before importing, then deletes the hash file.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Number of parallel hashing workers. Defaults to the CPU count.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress normal output; only print problems. Suitable for cron jobs.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-missing
Do not check for files that have been removed from disk.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-hidden
Include hidden files and directories (names starting with \fB.\fR),
which are excluded by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " PATH" \fR...
Exclude one or more directories. Paths may be relative to the target
directory or absolute.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Use a custom database path instead of the default location inside the
target directory.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All files verified OK.
.TP
.B 1
Missing files detected.
.TP
.B 2
Bit rot detected (checksum mismatch).
.TP
.B 3
Run was interrupted (safe to re-run).
.SH FILE STATUSES
.TP
.B OK
Checksum verified; file is intact.
.TP
.B NEW
File seen for the first time.
.TP
.B FAILED
Bit rot detected \(em hash changed without any metadata change.
.TP
.B MISSING
File was previously tracked but no longer exists on disk.
.SH EXAMPLES
Index all files in the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.B rotbyte
.RE
.PP
Full re-verify of an external drive:
.PP
.RS
.B rotbyte \-\-check /Volumes/Media
.RE
.PP
Weekly cron job (quiet mode, log errors):
.PP
.RS
.B 0 2 * * 0 rotbyte \-\-check \-q /data >> /var/log/rotbyte.log 2>&1
.RE
.PP
Accept a restored file:
.PP
.RS
.B rotbyte \-\-accept restored_file.mkv
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI . dirname _checksums.db
SQLite database storing checksums and metadata, created inside the
target directory.
.TP
.BI . dirname _checksums.db.lock
Lock file preventing concurrent runs.
.SH NOTES
.B rotbyte
uses BLAKE2b-512 for hashing, which is faster than SHA-256 while
providing equivalent collision resistance. Hashing is parallelized
across multiple processes for maximum throughput on multi-core systems.
.PP
Symlinks are not followed to prevent infinite loops.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.9 or later. macOS or Linux (uses
.BR fcntl (2)
for file locking).
.SH AUTHORS
Written for use with Homebrew.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR b2sum (1),
.BR sha256sum (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
